<title>FRANCE: TABLE-Lafarge H1 turnover up 21.7 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Lafarge H1 turnover up 21.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover			  19,320    vs   15,878</p>
<p>- of which</p>
<p>	Cement					 8,944    vs    7,271</p>
<p>	Concrete and granulates		  5,133    vs    4,202</p>
<p>	Plaster					2,109    vs    1,559</p>
<p>	Specialty materials			3,135    vs    2,846</p>
<p>NOTE - Building materials group Lafarge said in a statement that sales grew 6.9 percent on a comparable structure and exchange rate basis. Growth in activity was spurred partly by a relatively weak first half in 1996 but also by healthy 1997 markets in North America, eastern Europe and emerging economies, it said. However construction markets in western Europe continued to suffer from &quot;the weakness of public investments&quot;.</p>
</text>
